# Session handoff (explicit request only)

## When to run

| Trigger | Handoff? |
|---------|----------|
| User writes **SESSION HANDOFF** or asks to save session / persist context | **Yes** |
| Ordinary feature work, bugfix, or question answered | **No** |
| Agent turn finished with uncommitted git | **No** (stop hook does not auto-trigger) |

## Two memory files

| File | Purpose | When to update |
|------|---------|----------------|
| **`claude-current-remindifier-state.md`** | Session snapshot | **Only during explicit handoff** |
| **`PROJECT_MEMORY.md`** | Stable architecture | Only when conventions or structure change |

**Never** create ad-hoc context files unless the user asks.

## Handoff steps (when user requested)

1. Read **`claude-current-remindifier-state.md`** and **`PROJECT_MEMORY.md`** if not already loaded
2. Update state file: latest commit, what was done, uncommitted changes, user agreements
3. Update **`PROJECT_MEMORY.md`** only if architecture/routes/conventions changed
4. Stage and commit relevant files — **push only if the user asked** to push (see user git rules)
5. Do not commit: `.env`, `coverage/`, `expo-output.log`

## Session start (before work — not a handoff)

1. Read memory files (or use injected context from `sessionStart` hook)
2. `git pull --rebase origin sandbox` when starting substantive work

